  "match": ["3000f", "3000r", "3000 series", "marwin 3000", "high performance ball", "fire safe ball"],
  "source": { "doc": "3000-Full.pdf and 3000-Reduced.pdf", "page": 9, "section": "Ordering matrix, final page" },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering matrices on the final pages of the full port and reduced port sheets, which share every table; the port lives in the model number and the size ranges differ, full 1/4 to 3 inch, reduced 1/2 to 4 inch, held as constraints. The code reads an optional special-options prefix, model, size, body, then designators: ends 1&2, trim 3&4, seat 5&6, packing 7&8, handle 9&10, actuator 11&12, solenoid 13&14, then single characters for limit switch 15, positioner 16, fail position 17 and accessory 18. The price book's manual rows print only positions 1 to 10; the full ordering code continues to 18, and a bare manual build is the full code with the trailing zeros stated. The book's chlorine-clean adder has no prefix in this sheet's table, so it is not offered here. The seat table's own instruction couples PEEK seats to 6P trim, the firesafe prefix to the graphite seat and packing sets, solenoids and accessories to pneumatic actuators within their printed UT spans, positioners to their actuator type and span, and spring fail positions to spring return builds. Siemens is named per the CV3000 decision, an accessory openly listed in the public datasheet.",
